# ============================================================================
# Build context for deploy/gateway.Dockerfile.
#
# DENY EVERYTHING, then re-admit the four paths the image is built from. The
# inverse (listing what to exclude) fails open: a new `.env.staging`, a dumped
# database, or a downloaded IEEE-CIS archive would land in the context and then
# in a layer, and CLAUDE.md §9 forbids a secret in an image. It also keeps the
# context small -- `.venv/` and `data/` alone are the bulk of this working tree,
# and neither has any business being sent to the daemon.
# ============================================================================
*

# The project metadata and the pinned dependency set (ADR-0018 / `make lock`).
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.lock

# The modular monolith, installed as a package: its rule packs and threshold
# config ship as package data, so the gateway can boot on its own.
!packages

# The thin HTTP entrypoint. NOT part of the installed package
# ([tool.setuptools.packages.find] looks only in packages/), so it is copied and
# imported from the working directory.
!services

# Compiled artefacts of the host's Python, which is not the image's Python.
# Copying them in would leave stale bytecode shadowing the source it came from.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
